AssertionError: Regex didn't match: 'about \\w+\\s+minutes?\\s+\\(\\d+ tests, \\d+ s on \\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\)' not found in '# oh-dispatch (for developers)\n\noh-dispatch runs coding agents as gated workers. `ohflow` is its orchestrator. A plan holds phases, and a phase holds steps of kind `worker`, `command`, `gate` or `merge`. Each worker runs in its own git worktree on one lane: `pi`, `host`, `claude`, `codex` or `dsh`. The constructor is the gate. A worker calls only the tools it was built with. A gate checks the worker\'s artifact, because the worker\'s final message is a claim. Every run leaves a journal, a live dashboard and an exit report.\n\nAgents read [SKILL.md](SKILL.md). It routes by task and lists the verbs. Terms are in [CONTEXT.md](CONTEXT.md). Facts live in [references/](references/). This file is for people who change the code.\n\nHistory: [docs/history/](docs/history/) holds the design plans, the dated measurements and the earlier plans.\n\n## Module map\n\nEach deep module hides one fact behind a small interface. Callers use the interface and never read the files the module owns.\n\n- `lanes.py` hides which module owns each lane. Interface: `lane_module(name)` answers `worker_errors`, `usage`, `activity`, `resume_target`, `trace` and `make_lane`.\n- `cli_lane.CliAgentRuntime` hides the child process of a CLI lane. Interface: start, event log, heartbeat, stall deadline and kill.\n- `rundir.open_run(path)` hides the layout of a run directory. Interface: `run.steps()`, `run.attempts(coord)`, `run.latest_attempt(coord)`, `run.usage(attempt)`, `run.summary()`.\n- `attempt_record` hides what `result.json` holds. Interface: `write` and the token vocabulary `TOKEN_KEYS`.\n- `live.snapshot(run_dir, now)` hides the parsing of journal, logs and sessions. Interface: one JSON document that the dashboard and both exit reports show.\n- `runstatus.sentence` hides how a run is described. Interface: one status sentence and the `facts` a watcher compares.\n- `supervisor.run_plan` hides the start of a run. Interface: one function that reserves the run directory, starts the dashboard, runs the engine and writes the exit report.\n- `proc.spawn_managed` hides the Windows kill-on-close job object. Interface: start a child, then end its whole tree.\n- `exec` hides shell choice and log capture. Interface: run a command and get its exit code, log paths and a 4 KB tail.\n- `retry.should_retry` hides the retry rule. Interface: a pure function that returns a decision and its reason.\n- `failure.classify` hides the rate-limit signatures. Interface: error text in, `transient` or `structural` out.\n\nThe engine, the journal and the plan model sit beside these. The journal is the truth about a run.\n\n## Running the suite\n\nThe suite uses `unittest` from the standard library. It runs from a fresh clone and needs no network. A full run takes about fifteen minutes (911 tests, 857.8 s on 2026-10-02). Run it in three shards. Each shard stays under ten minutes.\n\nDeterministic. Each shard takes about five minutes (310.7 s, 290.1 s and 257.0 s on 2026-10-02):\n\n```bash\npython oh-dispatch/tests/run_tests.py --shard 1/3\npython oh-dispatch/tests/run_tests.py --shard 2/3\npython oh-dispatch/tests/run_tests.py --shard 3/3\n```\n\nDeterministic. `-k` takes one substring of a test name:\n\n```bash\npython oh-dispatch/tests/run_tests.py -k rollcall\n```\n\n`--e2e` adds the live smoke matrix. It needs `ZAI_CODING_CN_API_KEY` and `~/sdk/.venv`. See "Testing with live agents".\n\n**Add a regression test.** Name the file `tests/test_defect_NN_<what>.py` and put one defect in it. Take the helpers from `tests/support.py`: `TempCase`, `FakeLane`, `WorkerScript`, `git_repo`, `simple_plan`, `worker_step`, `stub_preflight`, `quiet`. Make the test fail first, then fix the code. Real provider errors go in `tests/fixtures/real_errors.py`. A test that pins a sentence in a document follows that sentence.\n\n## Testing with live agents\n\n`ohflow rollcall` is the one live harness. A roll call is a trivial task: each worker writes who it is, commits that file and ends with a JSON block in its final message. The lane records what its harness announced. The gate fails a final message that names a tool the harness never announced.\n\nA **cell** is one archetype on some lanes at some scale. A **matrix** is a named table of cells. Cells run one after another. Run the verb from `oh-dispatch/scripts`.\n\n### Archetypes\n\nEach archetype is a shape of the roll-call plan, chosen with the first word of a cell. The aliases `r0`, `r1` and `r2` mean `fanout`, `relay` and `merge`.\n\n| Shape | What it proves | Command |\n|---|---|---|\n| `single` | one gated worker finishes on one lane | `rollcall --cells single:pi` |\n| `fanout` | one worker per lane, each in its own worktree | `rollcall --cells fanout:pi,claude` |\n| `relay` | workers in series hand one shared file on | `rollcall --cells relay:pi,claude` |\n| `merge` | fanout, then one merge per worker, then a consolidator writes a table | `rollcall --cells merge:pi,claude:2:consolidator=codex` |\n| `retry` | a failed gate retries, and the retry reads the failure token in its position block | `rollcall --cells retry:pi` |\n| `review` | a worker on one lane, then a reviewer on another ends with a `VERDICT:` line | `rollcall --cells review:pi,claude` |\n| `campaign` | a judge revises a bad brief, the milestone then passes, and the trunk moves past its base | `rollcall --cells campaign:pi` |\n\nEvery command in this section starts with `cd oh-dispatch/scripts && PYTHONPATH=. python -m ohflow.cli`. A cell has the form `shape:lanes[:count][:option]`. The options are `consolidator`, `reviewer`, `judge` (each names a lane), the seat profile `profile=hermetic` (`claude` and `codex` only) and `carry_context`.\n\n### Routes\n\nA route is the lane, its model and its cost. Each lane\'s preflight runs before a cell. A lane that fails preflight, or whose `api_key_env` is unset, gives `SKIP` and not `FAIL`.\n\n| Lane | Default model | Preflight needs | Cost basis |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `pi` | `zai/glm-5.3-flash`, `thinking=low` | the pi CLI, Git Bash, `ZAI_CODING_CN_API_KEY` | Z.AI flat rate |\n| `host` | `openai/glm-5.3-flash` | `~/sdk/.venv`, `ZAI_CODING_CN_API_KEY` | Z.AI flat rate |\n| `claude` | `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` | the Claude CLI, logged in | seat subscription; `total_cost_usd` is notional |\n| `codex` | `gpt-5.6-luna`, `reasoning_effort=low` | the Codex CLI, logged in | ChatGPT seat quota |\n| `dsh` | the `headless` seat profile\'s model | the dsh CLI | Z.AI key, shared with `pi` |\n\nLane facts and launch rules: [lanes](references/lanes.md).\n\n### Scales\n\n- **`count`** is the number of workers per lane. `fanout:pi:3` starts three workers on `pi`.\n- **Parallelism** is the plan argument `max_parallel`. A matrix run keeps its default of 3.\n- **Wall and stall limits** are the plan arguments `wall_timeout_s` (default 600) and `stall_timeout_s`. The stall limit defaults per lane: 600 s for codex, 180 s for `pi`, `claude` and `dsh`. The `host` lane takes no stall limit. The argument replaces that table for every lane that takes a limit.\n\nPass plan arguments to `validate` and `run` with `--plan ohflow.plans.rollcall --args repo=<repo> --args shape=<shape>`.\n\n### Matrices\n\n`--matrix` takes a name. The default is `quick`. `--list` prints every cell of every matrix.\n\n| Matrix | Cells | Contents | Wall time |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `smoke` | 2 | `single` on `pi` and on `host` | `single pi` 31 s, `single host` 1 m 51 s (5.4 k and 87.0 k tokens, m5 acceptance run) |\n| `quick` | 10 | `single` on all five lanes; `fanout`, `relay` and `merge` on `pi`, `claude`, `codex`, `dsh`; `retry` on `pi`; `review` on `pi` then `claude` | 24 m 27 s (1466.5 s: the sum of these ten cells\' times in the first full matrix run on 2026-10-01, not a run of `quick`; 2 of the 10 failed before the m7 fixes) |\n| `full` | 15 | `quick`, plus `fanout` on `pi` with `count=3`, `campaign` on `pi`, `single` hermetic on `claude` and on `codex`, `retry` on `claude` with `carry_context` | 32 m 23 s (1942.7 s, same run; 3 of 15 cells failed before the m7 fixes) |\n\nCost: `smoke` runs on the Z.AI flat rate. `quick` and `full` also use the seat quotas of `claude` and `codex`. `run_tests.py --e2e` runs `smoke`.\n\nLive. This runs the smoke matrix:\n\n```bash\ncd oh-dispatch/scripts && PYTHONPATH=. python -m ohflow.cli rollcall --matrix smoke\n```\n\nDeterministic. These check every plan without starting a worker:\n\n```bash\ncd oh-dispatch/scripts && PYTHONPATH=. python -m ohflow.cli rollcall --list\ncd oh-dispatch/scripts && PYTHONPATH=. python -m ohflow.cli rollcall --matrix full --dry-run\ncd oh-dispatch/scripts && PYTHONPATH=. python -m ohflow.cli rollcall --cells merge:pi,claude:2:consolidator=codex --dry-run\n```\n\n### Read a matrix result\n\nEach cell prints one line, verdict first:\n\n    PASS single pi count=1  0m31s  5.4 k tokens  <run dir>\n    FAIL review pi,claude count=1  1m02s  9.0 k tokens  <run dir>  step reviewer: <check>\n    SKIP single claude count=1  claude lane: <why>\n\nA `FAIL` line ends with the first failing step and check. Read that run with `status --run <run dir>` and open its trace with `trace`. The last line is `ROLLCALL PASS: N of N cells` or `ROLLCALL FAIL: F of N cells failed, S skipped`. A run where every cell skipped reads `FAIL`. `--dry-run` prints one `PLAN` line per cell and ends with `ROLLCALL DRY: N cells valid`.\n\n| Exit | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | `ROLLCALL PASS` or `ROLLCALL DRY` |\n| 1 | `ROLLCALL FAIL` |\n| 2 | a bad cell, matrix or config |\n\nA passing cell has also proved its resume: resuming the finished run starts no step. The `campaign` cell does not check resume.\n\n`matrix.json` in `--out` is the heartbeat. It is rewritten after each cell, so a long run is readable while it goes. Each cell\'s run directory is `<out>/NN-<shape>-<lanes>-<count>/run`. Without `--repo`, the verb makes a throwaway repo with one commit under `--out`. Stdout carries only the verdicts. `-v` streams each run\'s own lines.\n\n### The A/B seam\n\n`--config FILE` overrides the model of any lane for the whole matrix:\n\n```json\n{"name": "haiku-vs-sonnet", "lanes": {"claude": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5"}}}\n```\n\nA lane entry may set `model`, `base_url`, `api_key_env`, `params` and `extra_body`. Comparing two configs is out of scope today. Run the same cells once per config file with a separate `--out`, then compare the two `matrix.json` files by hand.\n\n## Add a lane\n\nA lane is a module that answers six questions, plus one row in the registry.\n\n1. **Register it.** Add a `LaneInfo` row to `LANE_INFO` in `scripts/ohflow/lanes.py`. It names the module and the capabilities that validation reads.\n2. **Answer the lane questions** in the module: `worker_errors`, `usage`, `activity`, `resume_target`, `trace` and `make_lane`. `lanes.py` lists what each returns. `usage` answers in the vocabulary of `attempt_record.TOKEN_KEYS`.\n3. **Write a fake CLI** in `tests/fakes/fake_<lane>.py`, after the existing three. It replays a session recorded from the real CLI.\n4. **Record fixtures** under `tests/fixtures/<lane>/`: the real session, usage and error text.\n5. **Write the contract test** `tests/test_lane_contract_<lane>.py`. Take the shared assertions from `tests/contract_support.py`: usage equals the tokens in `result.json`, activity ends on the last tool call, a retry names its resume target or none, trace points at a file.\n6. **Add the roll-call route.** Put the lane\'s cheap model in `MODELS` in `scripts/ohflow/plans/rollcall.py`, and name it in `FIVE` and `FOUR` in `scripts/ohflow/rollcall.py`.\n7. **Run a live `single`.** The cell proves the lane end to end:\n\n```bash\ncd oh-dispatch/scripts && PYTHONPATH=. python -m ohflow.cli rollcall --cells single:<lane>\n```\n\nDone when the contract test passes and the live `single` prints `PASS`. Lane facts go in [lanes](references/lanes.md).\n\n## Add an archetype\n\nAn archetype is a shape of the roll-call plan.\n\n1. **Add the shape.** Name it in `SHAPES` in `scripts/ohflow/plans/rollcall.py` and build its phases there. Its gate checks the artifact, not the worker\'s words.\n2. **Add a deterministic test.** `tests/test_rollcall_01_shapes.py` builds each shape\'s plan and validates it. Copy its pattern, so a broken shape fails without a live agent.\n3. **Add a matrix row.** Put a `_cell(...)` in `MATRICES` in `scripts/ohflow/rollcall.py`. `rollcall --list` then shows it.\n4. **Update the tables** above: the archetype row and the cell count of each matrix that holds the new cell.\n\nDone when the new test passes, `rollcall --cells <shape>:pi --dry-run` prints `ROLLCALL DRY`, and one live cell prints `PASS`.\n'

